From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jens Fursund <jens@spectralcompute.co.uk>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 15:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Treat PCI class 0x1200 (processing accelerator) as a GPU

NCCL finds out what is at the other end of an NVLink by reading the
target's PCI class from sysfs, and only class 0x03 counts as a GPU.
Accelerators of class 0x1200 (processing accelerator: AMD Instinct
MI300A, MI300X, MI325X and MI355X all report it) fall back to PCI, and
ncclTopoAddNvLinks connects every link whose target is neither a GPU nor
a CPU to one virtual NVSwitch. A full mesh of such GPUs then looks like
an NVSwitch system: the search sees one switch with the sum of all link
bandwidth, keeps sameChannels=1 and repeats one ring order on every
channel, so each GPU sends over one of its links only.

With the class recognised, the links connect GPU to GPU, as on an NVLink
mesh of class 0x03 GPUs, and the ring search spreads distinct orders
over all links. A device of this class that isn't in the communicator
is left out, as for 0x03.

kvDictPciClass also types the nodes of the PCI tree (ncclTopoAddPci).
There a class 0x1200 node is now a GPU too, so, like a class 0x03 node,
it is only added when it has a <gpu> child. NVIDIA's GPUs (0x03) and
NVSwitches (0x068000) match earlier entries, so for them nothing
changes.

4x MI300A (xGMI full mesh), nccl-tests -g 4, 256 MiB, bus bandwidth:
the search goes from maxBw 240 / sameChannels 1 / one ring order to
maxBw 80 / sameChannels 0 / six ring orders; all_reduce 85 -> 151 GB/s,
all_gather 83 -> 147, reduce_scatter 80 -> 127, broadcast 87 -> 162,
reduce 86 -> 140.
---
diff --git a/src/graph/topo.cc b/src/graph/topo.cc
index 16d7372..6fc3c54 100644
--- a/src/graph/topo.cc
+++ b/src/graph/topo.cc
@@ -442,7 +442,7 @@ ncclResult_t ncclTopoAddGpu(struct ncclXmlNode* xmlGpu, struct ncclTopoSystem* s
 
 #define PCI_BRIDGE_DEVICE_CLASS "0x060400"
 
-struct kvDict kvDictPciClass[] = { { PCI_BRIDGE_DEVICE_CLASS, PCI }, {"0x080100", /*CX8 data direct*/PCI}, { "0x068000", NVS }, { "0x068001", CPU }, { "0x03", GPU }, { "0x02", NIC }, { NULL, PCI /* Default fallback value */ } };
+struct kvDict kvDictPciClass[] = { { PCI_BRIDGE_DEVICE_CLASS, PCI }, {"0x080100", /*CX8 data direct*/PCI}, { "0x068000", NVS }, { "0x068001", CPU }, { "0x03", GPU }, { "0x1200", /*Processing accelerator*/GPU }, { "0x02", NIC }, { NULL, PCI /* Default fallback value */ } };
 struct kvDict kvDictPciGen[] = {
   { "2.5 GT/s", 15 }, { "5 GT/s", 30 }, { "8 GT/s", 60 }, { "16 GT/s", 120 }, { "32 GT/s", 240 }, /* Kernel 5.6 and earlier */
   { "2.5 GT/s PCIe", 15 }, { "5.0 GT/s PCIe", 30 }, { "8.0 GT/s PCIe", 60 }, { "16.0 GT/s PCIe", 120 }, { "32.0 GT/s PCIe", 240 }, { "64.0 GT/s PCIe", 480 },
